ies, making it the United Kingdom's 39th most populous built-up area. Aberdeen has a long, sandy coastline and features an oceanic climate, with cool summers and mild, rainy winters.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/%2B_%22Silver_City%22_wird_Aberdeen_wegen_seiner_vielen_Granitgeb%C3%A4ude_genannt._07.jpg/330px-%2B_%22Silver_City%22_wird_Aberdeen_wegen_seiner_vielen_Granitgeb%C3%A4ude_genannt._07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aberdeen"},"twins":["Q25416","Q486913","Q2978","Q42168","Q193250","Q16555","Q2678","Q9248","Q62823"],"climate":{"temp":[5.9,5.3,5.8,7.1,9.2,11.7,13.8,14,12.9,11,8.7,6.8],"rain":[86,69,64,50,50,71,75,84,61,109,99,88],"cloud":[79,78,78,75,76,84,84,82,77,76,76,78]}}